IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ppl-logic`
IMPORT `ppl-time`
IMPORT `ppl-nouns`
IMPORT `ppl-definitions`
IMPORT `ppl-key-provisions`

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Commonwealth), compilation C2026C00425, Chapter 2 Part 2-2 (sections 12 to 29): determinations about whether parental leave pay is payable.
-- Section 12 is a guide to the Part and states no rule of its own.
-- "The Secretary is satisfied that X" is encoded as X on the facts as stated.
-- A duty with an "if" that is not met answers NOTHING; a bar ("must not make", "cannot") answers JUST FALSE when it applies and NOTHING when it does not.
-- A requirement ("must be given", "must state") answers JUST TRUE when every item is met and JUST FALSE when one is not.

-- Division 2: the determinations themselves

-- src:417 | (3) The following persons are covered by this subsection:
-- src:418 | (a) a person who:
-- src:419 | (i) is a parent (other than an adoptive parent) of the child; and
-- src:420 | (ii) is not the child’s birth mother;
-- src:421 | (b) the partner of the child’s birth mother;
-- src:422 | (c) the partner of a person covered by paragraph (a).
@ref s 13(3) (src:417-422)
GIVEN r IS A `The parental relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is covered by subsection 13(3)` MEANS
       ((`the person is a parent of the child, taking the ordinary sense where the Dictionary gives none` r) AND (NOT (r's `the person is an adoptive parent of the child`)) AND (NOT (r's `the person is the child's birth mother`)))
    OR (r's `the person is the partner of the child's birth mother`)
    OR (r's `the person is the partner of a person covered by section 13(3)(a)`)

-- src:423 | (4) The following persons are covered by this subsection:
-- src:424 | (a) an adoptive parent of the child, if a payability determination under this section that parental leave pay for the child is payable is in force in relation to another adoptive parent of the child;
-- src:425 | (b) the partner of an adoptive parent of the child.
@ref s 13(4) (src:423-425)
GIVEN r IS A `The parental relationship`
      `a payability determination under section 13 is in force in relation to another adoptive parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is covered by subsection 13(4)` MEANS
       ((r's `the person is an adoptive parent of the child`) AND `a payability determination under section 13 is in force in relation to another adoptive parent of the child`)
    OR (r's `the person is the partner of an adoptive parent of the child`)

GIVEN p IS A `A permission to claim flexible PPL days`
      `the number of flexible PPL days for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person if the determination were made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a permission is in place and covers the number of days` MEANS
    JUST (        (p's `a permission has been given`)
          AND (NOT (p's `the permission has been revoked`))
          AND (`the number of flexible PPL days for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person if the determination were made` AT MOST (p's `the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission`)))

-- src:393 | (1) If:
-- src:394 | (a) a PPL claimant has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child; and
-- src:395 | (b) one or more flexible PPL days for the child (the claimed days) have been specified in the claim;
-- src:396 | the Secretary must make a determination on the PPL claim under this section.
@ref s 13(1) (src:393-396)
GIVEN `a PPL claimant has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more flexible PPL days for the child have been specified in the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must make a determination on the PPL claim under section 13` MEANS
    IF `a PPL claimant has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child` AND `one or more flexible PPL days for the child have been specified in the claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:398 | (2) The Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is payable to the PPL claimant for one or more of the claimed days if, when making the determination, the Secretary is satisfied that:
-- src:399 | (a) the PPL claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on those days; and
-- src:400 | (b) if:
-- src:401 | (i) the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (3); and
-- src:402 | (ii) the child’s birth mother has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child;
-- src:403 | the child’s birth mother satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made; and
-- src:404 | (c) if:
-- src:405 | (i) the PPL claimant is the partner of an adoptive parent of the child; and
-- src:406 | (ii) an adoptive parent of the child has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child;
-- src:407 | the person who gave the PPL claimant the permission referred to in subparagraph (e)(i) satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made; and
-- src:408 | (d) if the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (3) and the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph do not apply to the PPL claimant:
-- src:409 | (i) a permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(a) in relation to the child; and
-- src:410 | (ii) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:411 | (iii) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission; and
-- src:412 | (e) if the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (4) and the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph do not apply to the PPL claimant:
-- src:413 | (i) a permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(b) or (c) in relation to the child; and
-- src:414 | (ii) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:415 | (iii) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission.
@ref s 13(2) (src:398-415)
GIVEN r IS A `The parental relationship`
      f IS A `The facts for a determination under section 13(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is payable under section 13(2)` MEANS
    `every result in a list holds` (LIST paragraphA, paragraphB, paragraphC, paragraphD, paragraphE)
    WHERE
        coveredBy3 MEANS `a person is covered by subsection 13(3)` r
        coveredBy4 MEANS `a person is covered by subsection 13(4)` r (f's `a payability determination under section 13 is in force in relation to another adoptive parent of the child`)
        paragraphA MEANS f's `the claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on the claimed days`
        paragraphB MEANS
            IF coveredBy3 AND (f's `the child's birth mother has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child`)
            THEN f's `the child's birth mother satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made`
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        paragraphC MEANS
            IF (r's `the person is the partner of an adoptive parent of the child`) AND (f's `an adoptive parent of the child has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child`)
            THEN f's `the person who gave the claimant the permission referred to in subparagraph 13(2)(e)(i) satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made`
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        paragraphD MEANS
            IF coveredBy3 AND (NOT (f's `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(d) apply to the claimant`))
            THEN `a permission is in place and covers the number of days` (f's `the permission given to the claimant under paragraph 15(1)(a)`) (f's `the number of flexible PPL days for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person if the determination were made`)
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        paragraphE MEANS
            IF coveredBy4 AND (NOT (f's `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(e) apply to the claimant`))
            THEN `a permission is in place and covers the number of days` (f's `the permission given to the claimant under paragraph 15(1)(b) or (c)`) (f's `the number of flexible PPL days for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person if the determination were made`)
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:408 | (d) if the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (3) and the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph do not apply to the PPL claimant:
-- src:409 | (i) a permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(a) in relation to the child; and
-- src:410 | (ii) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:411 | (iii) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission; and
-- src:412 | (e) if the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (4) and the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph do not apply to the PPL claimant:
-- src:413 | (i) a permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(b) or (c) in relation to the child; and
-- src:414 | (ii) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:415 | (iii) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission.
@ref s 13(2)(d) and (e) (src:408-415)
GIVEN r IS A `The parental relationship`
      `a payability determination under section 13 is in force in relation to another adoptive parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(d) apply to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(e) apply to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a permission is needed before the Secretary can determine a PPL claim` MEANS
       ((`a person is covered by subsection 13(3)` r) AND (NOT `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(d) apply to the claimant`))
    OR ((`a person is covered by subsection 13(4)` r `a payability determination under section 13 is in force in relation to another adoptive parent of the child`) AND (NOT `the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph 13(2)(e) apply to the claimant`))

-- src:428 | (6) If the Secretary is not satisfied of the matters in subsection (2) for one or more of the claimed days, the Secretary must:
-- src:429 | (a) determine that parental leave pay is not payable to the PPL claimant for those days; and
@ref s 13(6)(a) (src:428-429)
GIVEN `the result under section 13(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is not payable under section 13(6)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the result under section 13(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:430 | (b) if:
-- src:431 | (i) the PPL claimant has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child; and
-- src:432 | (ii) the Secretary is satisfied that the PPL claimant satisfies the work test and income test on the day the determination is made;
-- src:433 | determine that the PPL claimant is conditionally eligible for parental leave pay for other flexible PPL days for the child.
@ref s 13(6)(b) (src:430-433)
GIVEN `the result under section 13(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that the claimant satisfies the work test and income test on the day the determination is made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must determine that the claimant is conditionally eligible under section 13(6)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the result under section 13(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN (IF `the claimant has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child`
          THEN `the Secretary is satisfied that the claimant satisfies the work test and income test on the day the determination is made`
          ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:437 | (1) If:
-- src:438 | (a) a special PPL claimant has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child; and
-- src:439 | (b) one or more flexible PPL days for the child (the claimed days) have been specified in the claim;
-- src:440 | the Secretary must make a determination on the special PPL claim under this section.
@ref s 14(1) (src:437-440)
GIVEN `a special PPL claimant has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more flexible PPL days for the child have been specified in the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must make a determination on the special PPL claim under section 14` MEANS
    IF `a special PPL claimant has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for a child` AND `one or more flexible PPL days for the child have been specified in the claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:442 | (2) The Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is payable to the special PPL claimant for one or more of the claimed days if, when making the determination, the Secretary is satisfied that:
-- src:443 | (a) a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable to a PPL claimant is in force; and
-- src:444 | (b) the special PPL claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on those days; and
-- src:445 | (c) if the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made—a permission has been given to the special PPL claimant under subsection 15(2) in relation to the child; and
-- src:446 | (d) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:447 | (e) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission.
@ref s 14(2) (src:442-447)
GIVEN f IS A `The facts for a determination under section 14(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is payable under section 14(2)` MEANS
    `every result in a list holds`
        (LIST JUST (f's `a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable to a PPL claimant is in force`)
            , f's `the special PPL claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on the claimed days`
            , paragraphC
            , paragraphD
            , paragraphE)
    WHERE
        permission MEANS f's `the permission given to the special PPL claimant under subsection 15(2)`
        paragraphC MEANS
            IF f's `the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`
            THEN JUST (permission's `a permission has been given`)
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        paragraphD MEANS
            IF permission's `a permission has been given` THEN JUST (NOT (permission's `the permission has been revoked`)) ELSE NOTHING
        paragraphE MEANS
            IF permission's `a permission has been given`
            THEN JUST ((f's `the number of flexible PPL days for which parental leave pay would be payable to the special PPL claimant if the determination were made`) AT MOST (permission's `the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission`))
            ELSE NOTHING

-- src:445 | (c) if the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made—a permission has been given to the special PPL claimant under subsection 15(2) in relation to the child; and
@ref s 14(2)(c) (src:445-445)
GIVEN `the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a permission is needed before the Secretary can determine a special PPL claim` MEANS
    `the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made`

-- src:426 | (5) The Secretary must specify in a determination made under subsection (2) the claimed days for which parental leave pay is payable to the PPL claimant.
-- src:427 | When parental leave pay is not payable to the PPL claimant for one or more claimed days
@ref s 13(5) (src:426-427)
GIVEN claimed IS A LIST OF `A claimed day`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the claimed days that a determination under section 13(2) must specify as payable` MEANS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the day claimed`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the Secretary is satisfied of the matters for the day`) claimed)

-- src:434 | (7) The Secretary must specify in the determination made under subsection (6) the claimed days for which parental leave pay is not payable to the PPL claimant.
@ref s 13(7) (src:434-434)
GIVEN claimed IS A LIST OF `A claimed day`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the claimed days that a determination under section 13(6) must specify as not payable` MEANS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the day claimed`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD (NOT (c's `the Secretary is satisfied of the matters for the day`))) claimed)

-- src:449 | (3) The Secretary must specify in the determination made under subsection (2) the claimed days for which parental leave pay is payable to the special PPL claimant.
-- src:450 | When parental leave pay is not payable to the special PPL claimant for the claimed days
@ref s 14(3) (src:449-450)
GIVEN claimed IS A LIST OF `A claimed day`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the claimed days that a determination under section 14(2) must specify as payable` MEANS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the day claimed`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the Secretary is satisfied of the matters for the day`) claimed)

-- src:458 | (5) The Secretary must specify in the determination made under subsection (4) the claimed days for which parental leave pay is not payable to the special PPL claimant.
@ref s 14(5) (src:458-458)
GIVEN claimed IS A LIST OF `A claimed day`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the claimed days that a determination under section 14(4) must specify as not payable` MEANS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the day claimed`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD (NOT (c's `the Secretary is satisfied of the matters for the day`))) claimed)

-- src:451 | (4) If the Secretary is not satisfied of the matters in subsection (2) for one or more of the claimed days, the Secretary must:
-- src:452 | (a) determine that parental leave pay is not payable to the special PPL claimant for those days; and
@ref s 14(4)(a) (src:451-452)
GIVEN `the result under section 14(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is not payable under section 14(4)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the result under section 14(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:453 | (b) if:
-- src:454 | (i) the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:455 | (ii) the special PPL claimant has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child; and
-- src:456 | (iii) the Secretary is satisfied that the special PPL claimant satisfies the work test and income test on the day the determination is made;
-- src:457 | determine that the special PPL claimant is conditionally eligible for parental leave pay for other flexible PPL days for the child.
@ref s 14(4)(b) (src:453-457)
GIVEN `the result under section 14(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special PPL claimant has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that the special PPL claimant satisfies the work test and income test on the day the determination is made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must determine that the special PPL claimant is conditionally eligible under section 14(4)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the result under section 14(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN (IF `the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` AND `the special PPL claimant has not previously satisfied the work and income tests in relation to the child`
          THEN `the Secretary is satisfied that the special PPL claimant satisfies the work test and income test on the day the determination is made`
          ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:461 | (1) Permission for PPL claimants to claim parental leave pay for one or more flexible PPL days for a child may be given by the following persons:
-- src:462 | (a) the child’s birth mother;
-- src:463 | (b) a person:
-- src:464 | (i) who is an adoptive parent of the child; and
-- src:465 | (ii) in respect of whom a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable is in force; and
-- src:466 | (iii) who is the first adoptive parent of the child in respect of whom a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable has been made;
-- src:467 | (c) an adoptive parent of the child who is nominated by the partner of an adoptive parent of the child to give permission to that partner.
@ref s 15(1) (src:461-467)
GIVEN `the person is the child's birth mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an adoptive parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable is in force in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the first adoptive parent of the child in respect of whom such a determination has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an adoptive parent of the child nominated by the partner of an adoptive parent of the child to give permission to that partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person may give permission to a PPL claimant under subsection 15(1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is the child's birth mother`
       OR (`the person is an adoptive parent of the child` AND `a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable is in force in respect of the person` AND `the person is the first adoptive parent of the child in respect of whom such a determination has been made`)
       OR `the person is an adoptive parent of the child nominated by the partner of an adoptive parent of the child to give permission to that partner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:468 | (2) Permission for special PPL claimants to claim parental leave pay for flexible PPL days for a child may be given by a person:
-- src:469 | (a) who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made; and
-- src:470 | (b) in respect of whom a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable is in force.
@ref s 15(2) (src:468-470)
GIVEN `the person satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable is in force in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person may give permission to a special PPL claimant under subsection 15(2)` MEANS
    IF `the person satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made` AND `a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable is in force in respect of the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:471 | (3) The permission must:
-- src:472 | (a) be given to the Secretary in the form approved by the Secretary; and
-- src:473 | (b) specify the number of flexible PPL days for the child to whom the permission relates that may be claimed; and
-- src:474 | (c) specify the person to whom the permission is given.
@ref s 15(3) (src:471-474)
GIVEN `the permission is given to the Secretary in the form approved by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permission specifies the number of flexible PPL days for the child that may be claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permission specifies the person to whom it is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a permission meets the requirements of subsection 15(3)` MEANS
    JUST (`the permission is given to the Secretary in the form approved by the Secretary` AND `the permission specifies the number of flexible PPL days for the child that may be claimed` AND `the permission specifies the person to whom it is given`)

-- src:478 | (4) If a person has given a permission under subsection (1) or (2), the person may:
-- src:479 | (a) vary the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in the permission; or
-- src:480 | (b) revoke the permission.
@ref s 15(4) (src:478-480)
GIVEN `the person has given a permission under subsection 15(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person may vary or revoke a permission they have given` MEANS
    IF `the person has given a permission under subsection 15(1) or (2)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:481 | (5) The variation or revocation must be given to the Secretary in the form approved by the Secretary.
@ref s 15(5) (src:481-481)
GIVEN `the variation or revocation is given to the Secretary in the form approved by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a variation or revocation of a permission meets the requirement of subsection 15(5)` MEANS
    JUST `the variation or revocation is given to the Secretary in the form approved by the Secretary`

-- src:482 | (6) If:
-- src:483 | (a) a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for one or more flexible PPL days for a child is in force in relation to a claim; and
-- src:484 | (b) permission was given in relation to that claim under subsection (1) or (2); and
-- src:485 | (c) that permission is varied under paragraph (4)(a);
-- src:486 | then:
-- src:487 | (d) the variation of the permission does not affect the operation of the payability determination in relation to the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is varied, have already occurred; and
-- src:488 | (e) the Secretary must vary the payability determination to remove the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is varied:
-- src:489 | (i) have not yet occurred; and
-- src:490 | (ii) exceed the number of days specified in the permission, as varied; and
-- src:491 | (f) the Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is not payable to the person for the days referred to in paragraph (e).
@ref s 15(6) (src:482-491)
GIVEN `a payability determination for one or more flexible PPL days is in force in relation to a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `permission was given in relation to that claim under subsection 15(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that permission is varied under paragraph 15(4)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days specified in the determination` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those days that have not yet occurred when the permission is varied` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days specified in the permission, as varied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of days the Secretary must remove from the determination when a permission is varied` MEANS
    IF `a payability determination for one or more flexible PPL days is in force in relation to a claim` AND `permission was given in relation to that claim under subsection 15(1) or (2)` AND `that permission is varied under paragraph 15(4)(a)`
    THEN JUST (`the number of days removed from the determination on a variation` `the number of days specified in the determination` `the number of those days that have not yet occurred when the permission is varied` `the number of days specified in the permission, as varied`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:493 | (7) If:
-- src:494 | (a) a payability determination is in force in relation to a claim made by a person; and
-- src:495 | (b) permission was given in relation to that claim under subsection (1) or (2); and
-- src:496 | (c) that permission is revoked in relation to the person under paragraph (4)(b);
-- src:497 | then:
-- src:498 | (d) the revocation of the permission does not affect the operation of the payability determination in relation to the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is revoked, have already occurred; and
-- src:499 | (e) the Secretary must vary the payability determination to remove the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is revoked, have not yet occurred; and
-- src:500 | (f) the Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is not payable to the person for the days referred to in paragraph (e).
@ref s 15(7) (src:493-500)
GIVEN `a payability determination is in force in relation to a claim made by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `permission was given in relation to that claim under subsection 15(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that permission is revoked under paragraph 15(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days specified in the determination that have not yet occurred when the permission is revoked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of days the Secretary must remove from the determination when a permission is revoked` MEANS
    IF `a payability determination is in force in relation to a claim made by the person` AND `permission was given in relation to that claim under subsection 15(1) or (2)` AND `that permission is revoked under paragraph 15(4)(b)`
    THEN JUST `the number of days specified in the determination that have not yet occurred when the permission is revoked`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Division 3: when the Secretary cannot make a determination

-- src:504 | (1) The Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a child unless a PPL claimant has verified the child’s birth.
@ref s 18(1) (src:504-504)
GIVEN `a PPL claimant has verified the child's birth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary can make a payability determination, as section 18 bears on it` MEANS
    IF `a PPL claimant has verified the child's birth` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:506 | (2) A person verifies a child’s birth if:
-- src:507 | (a) the person gives the Secretary a completed birth verification form for the child; and
-- src:508 | (b) if subsection (3) applies to the person, the person satisfies the requirement of that subsection.
-- src:509 | (3) If:
-- src:510 | (a) the person is the parent (other than an adoptive parent) of the child; and
-- src:511 | (b) the child is not stillborn; and
-- src:512 | (c) the person is, under a law of a State or a Territory, responsible (whether alone or jointly) for registering the birth of the child under the law;
-- src:513 | then the person must give the Secretary information showing that:
-- src:514 | (d) the child’s birth has been registered under the law; or
-- src:515 | (e) the person has applied to have the birth of the child registered under the law.
@ref s 18(2)-(3) (src:506-515)
GIVEN `the person gives the Secretary a completed birth verification form for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a parent of the child other than an adoptive parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is not stillborn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is, under a law of a State or a Territory, responsible for having the birth of the child entered in the official record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives the Secretary information showing that the child's birth has been entered in the official record under the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives the Secretary information showing that the person has applied to have the birth of the child entered in the official record under the law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person verifies a child's birth` MEANS
    JUST (        `the person gives the Secretary a completed birth verification form for the child`
          AND (   (NOT subsection3Applies)
               OR `the person gives the Secretary information showing that the child's birth has been entered in the official record under the law`
               OR `the person gives the Secretary information showing that the person has applied to have the birth of the child entered in the official record under the law`))
    WHERE
        subsection3Applies MEANS `the person is a parent of the child other than an adoptive parent` AND `the child is not stillborn` AND `the person is, under a law of a State or a Territory, responsible for having the birth of the child entered in the official record`

-- src:516 | (4) The Secretary may approve a form (a birth verification form) for the purposes of verifying the birth of a child.
@ref s 18(4) (src:516-516)
GIVEN `the Secretary has approved the form for the purposes of verifying the birth of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a form is a birth verification form` MEANS
    JUST `the Secretary has approved the form for the purposes of verifying the birth of a child`

-- src:518 | If a person is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for a child of the person, the Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to the person for the child if the child is born after 31 March 2021.
@ref s 19B (src:518-518)
GIVEN `the person is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      born IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary can make a payability determination, as section 19B bears on it` MEANS
    IF `the person is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for the child` AND `a child is born after 31 March 2021` born
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:520 | The Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a child if:
-- src:521 | (a) the child and another child are born during the same multiple birth; and
-- src:522 | (b) parental leave pay is or was payable to the person or another person for the other child.
@ref s 20 (src:520-522)
GIVEN `the child and another child are born during the same multiple birth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `parental leave pay is or was payable to the person or another person for the other child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary can make a payability determination, as section 20 bears on it` MEANS
    IF `the child and another child are born during the same multiple birth` AND `parental leave pay is or was payable to the person or another person for the other child`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:524 | (1) The Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day (the relevant day) for a child if:
-- src:525 | (a) the effect of one or more payability determinations made by the Secretary under section 13 or 14 is that parental leave pay is payable to more than one person for the same flexible PPL day for the child on a total of:
-- src:526 | (i) if the child is born before 1 July 2025—10 flexible PPL days; or
-- src:527 | (ii) if the child is born on or after 1 July 2025—20 flexible PPL days; and
-- src:528 | (b) the effect of a payability determination made by the Secretary under section 13 or 14 is that parental leave pay is payable to another person for the relevant day.
-- src:529 | (2) However, the PPL rules may prescribe circumstances in which a flexible PPL day does not count towards the total number of flexible PPL days referred to in paragraph (1)(a).
@ref s 21 (src:524-529)
GIVEN `the number of flexible PPL days that count for which parental leave pay is payable to more than one person for the same flexible PPL day` IS A NUMBER
      `a payability determination makes parental leave pay payable to another person for the relevant day` IS A BOOLEAN
      born IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary can make a payability determination, as section 21 bears on it` MEANS
    IF `the number of flexible PPL days that count for which parental leave pay is payable to more than one person for the same flexible PPL day` AT LEAST (`the total of flexible PPL days for more than one person, for a child born on` born)
       AND `a payability determination makes parental leave pay payable to another person for the relevant day`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:371 | The Secretary cannot make a determination under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day for a child unless the person was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on that day.
-- src:374 | The Secretary cannot make a determination under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day for a child unless the person has made:
-- src:375 | (a) an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day (in which case the person is a PPL claimant); or
-- src:376 | (b) an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day (in which case the person is a special PPL claimant).
-- src:398 | (2) The Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is payable to the PPL claimant for one or more of the claimed days if, when making the determination, the Secretary is satisfied that:
-- src:399 | (a) the PPL claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on those days; and
-- src:400 | (b) if:
-- src:401 | (i) the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (3); and
-- src:402 | (ii) the child’s birth mother has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child;
-- src:403 | the child’s birth mother satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made; and
-- src:404 | (c) if:
-- src:405 | (i) the PPL claimant is the partner of an adoptive parent of the child; and
-- src:406 | (ii) an adoptive parent of the child has not previously satisfied the work test in relation to the child;
-- src:407 | the person who gave the PPL claimant the permission referred to in subparagraph (e)(i) satisfies the work test on the day the determination is made; and
-- src:408 | (d) if the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (3) and the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph do not apply to the PPL claimant:
-- src:409 | (i) a permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(a) in relation to the child; and
-- src:410 | (ii) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:411 | (iii) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission; and
-- src:412 | (e) if the PPL claimant is a person covered by subsection (4) and the circumstances prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph do not apply to the PPL claimant:
-- src:413 | (i) a permission has been given to the PPL claimant under paragraph 15(1)(b) or (c) in relation to the child; and
-- src:414 | (ii) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:415 | (iii) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission.
-- src:442 | (2) The Secretary must determine that parental leave pay is payable to the special PPL claimant for one or more of the claimed days if, when making the determination, the Secretary is satisfied that:
-- src:443 | (a) a payability determination under section 13 that parental leave pay for the child is payable to a PPL claimant is in force; and
-- src:444 | (b) the special PPL claimant was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on those days; and
-- src:445 | (c) if the special PPL claimant is the partner of a person who satisfies the circumstances prescribed by the PPL rules as being exceptional circumstances in which a PPL claim can be made—a permission has been given to the special PPL claimant under subsection 15(2) in relation to the child; and
-- src:446 | (d) the permission has not been revoked; and
-- src:447 | (e) if the determination were made, the number of flexible PPL days for the child for which parental leave pay would be payable to the person would not exceed the number of flexible PPL days specified in the permission.
-- src:504 | (1) The Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a child unless a PPL claimant has verified the child’s birth.
-- src:518 | If a person is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for a child of the person, the Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to the person for the child if the child is born after 31 March 2021.
-- src:520 | The Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a child if:
-- src:521 | (a) the child and another child are born during the same multiple birth; and
-- src:522 | (b) parental leave pay is or was payable to the person or another person for the other child.
-- src:524 | (1) The Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day (the relevant day) for a child if:
-- src:525 | (a) the effect of one or more payability determinations made by the Secretary under section 13 or 14 is that parental leave pay is payable to more than one person for the same flexible PPL day for the child on a total of:
-- src:526 | (i) if the child is born before 1 July 2025—10 flexible PPL days; or
-- src:527 | (ii) if the child is born on or after 1 July 2025—20 flexible PPL days; and
-- src:528 | (b) the effect of a payability determination made by the Secretary under section 13 or 14 is that parental leave pay is payable to another person for the relevant day.
@ref s 11B, 11C, 13(2), 14(2), 18, 19B, 20, 21 (src:371-528)
GIVEN `the result under section 13(2) or 14(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the results of the provisions that bar a determination` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary can determine that parental leave pay is payable` MEANS
    IF count (filter (GIVEN b YIELD b EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the results of the provisions that bar a determination`) GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `the result under section 13(2) or 14(2)`

-- Division 4: general provisions

GIVEN day IS A DATE, `the end day` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day is before an end day that may not exist` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the end day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST d THEN day LESS THAN d

-- src:532 | In deciding whether to make a payability determination about parental leave pay, the Secretary may act on the assumption that the state of affairs known to the Secretary when making the determination will remain unchanged.
@ref s 22 (src:532-532)
GIVEN `the Secretary is deciding whether to make a payability determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary may act on the assumption that the state of affairs known will remain unchanged, for a payability determination` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary is deciding whether to make a payability determination` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:534 | A payability determination about parental leave pay comes into force on the day it is made and continues in force unless it is:
-- src:535 | (a) revoked under section 25 (which deals with revoking a payability determination on the claimant’s request); or
-- src:536 | (b) set aside under Chapter 5 (which deals with review of decisions).
@ref s 23 (src:534-536)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day the determination is made` IS A DATE
      `the day a revocation under section 25 comes into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the first day on which the determination is no longer in force because it is set aside under Chapter 5` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a payability determination is in force on a day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `the day a payability determination comes into force` `the day the determination is made`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `a day is before an end day that may not exist` day `the day a revocation under section 25 comes into force`
         AND `a day is before an end day that may not exist` day `the first day on which the determination is no longer in force because it is set aside under Chapter 5`

-- src:538 | If the Secretary makes a payability determination about parental leave pay for a child, the Secretary must give the claimant a notice stating:
-- src:539 | (a) whether parental leave pay is payable; and
-- src:540 | (c) if parental leave pay is payable for one or more flexible PPL days for the child—those days; and
-- src:541 | (d) if parental leave pay is not payable—whether a conditional eligibility determination has been made; and
-- src:542 | (e) that the claimant may apply for review of the determination in the manner set out in Chapter 5.
@ref s 24 (src:538-542)
GIVEN `the notice states whether parental leave pay is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `parental leave pay is payable for one or more flexible PPL days for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states those days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states whether a conditional eligibility determination has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the claimant may apply for review of the determination in the manner set out in Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a notice of a payability determination meets section 24` MEANS
    JUST (        `the notice states whether parental leave pay is payable`
          AND ((NOT `parental leave pay is payable for one or more flexible PPL days for the child`) OR `the notice states those days`)
          AND (`parental leave pay is payable for one or more flexible PPL days for the child` OR `the notice states whether a conditional eligibility determination has been made`)
          AND `the notice states that the claimant may apply for review of the determination in the manner set out in Chapter 5`)

-- src:544 | (1) If:
-- src:545 | (a) a payability determination is made that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day for a child; and
-- src:546 | (b) the person requests the Secretary to revoke the determination; and
-- src:547 | (c) the request is made before the last day of the instalment period for the instalment that relates to the flexible PPL day for the child; and
-- src:548 | (d) the request is made in a manner approved by the Secretary;
-- src:549 | then the Secretary must revoke the determination.
@ref s 25(1) (src:544-549)
GIVEN `a payability determination is made that parental leave pay is payable to the person for a flexible PPL day for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requests the Secretary to revoke the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the instalment period for the instalment that relates to the flexible PPL day for the child` IS A DATE
      `the request is made in a manner approved by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary must revoke the determination on request` MEANS
    IF        `a payability determination is made that parental leave pay is payable to the person for a flexible PPL day for the child`
          AND `the person requests the Secretary to revoke the determination`
          AND `a request to revoke is made before the last day of the instalment period` `the day of the request` `the last day of the instalment period for the instalment that relates to the flexible PPL day for the child`
          AND `the request is made in a manner approved by the Secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Division 5: initial eligibility determinations

-- src:553 | The Secretary may make a determination (the initial eligibility determination) that a person is initially eligible for parental leave pay for one or more flexible PPL days for a child if:
-- src:554 | (a) the flexible PPL days for the child are specified in an effective PPL claim or effective special PPL claim made by the person; and
-- src:555 | (b) if no other initial eligibility determination under this section is in force in relation to the person and child—the Secretary is satisfied that the person satisfies the work test and income test when making the determination; and
-- src:556 | (c) the Secretary is satisfied that the person satisfies the Australian residency test when making the determination.
@ref s 26A (src:553-556)
GIVEN `the flexible PPL days are specified in an effective PPL claim or effective special PPL claim made by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other initial eligibility determination under section 26A is in force in relation to the person and child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that the person satisfies the work test and income test when making the determination` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that the person satisfies the Australian residency test when making the determination` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary may make an initial eligibility determination` MEANS
    IF `the conditions of section 26A are all met` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the conditions of section 26A are all met` MEANS
            `every result in a list holds`
                (LIST JUST `the flexible PPL days are specified in an effective PPL claim or effective special PPL claim made by the person`
                    , (IF `no other initial eligibility determination under section 26A is in force in relation to the person and child`
                       THEN `the Secretary is satisfied that the person satisfies the work test and income test when making the determination`
                       ELSE JUST TRUE)
                    , `the Secretary is satisfied that the person satisfies the Australian residency test when making the determination`)

-- src:558 | In deciding whether to make an initial eligibility determination about parental leave pay, the Secretary may act on the assumption that the state of affairs known to the Secretary when making the determination will remain unchanged.
@ref s 27 (src:558-558)
GIVEN `the Secretary is deciding whether to make an initial eligibility determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary may act on the assumption that the state of affairs known will remain unchanged, for an initial eligibility determination` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary is deciding whether to make an initial eligibility determination` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:562 | If the Secretary makes an initial eligibility determination about parental leave pay, the Secretary must give a notice of the determination to the claimant.
@ref s 29 (src:562-562)
GIVEN `the Secretary has given the claimant a notice of the initial eligibility determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary has met the duty to give notice of an initial eligibility determination` MEANS
    JUST `the Secretary has given the claimant a notice of the initial eligibility determination`
